id: pm-slack-standup-v5q6
title: Declaring the pm CLI as a runtime dependency gives consumers a second nested copy whenever their host pin differs
description: "This package declared @unbrained/pm-cli in both dependencies and peerDependencies. The two ranges were separately satisfiable, so npm resolved them independently rather than treating the host copy as the one that counts: a consumer whose host pin sits below the dependency range while still inside the declared peer range receives their copy at the tree root plus a second, newer copy nested under this package. npm dedupes only when the ranges happen to overlap, so the tree is clean for some host pins and skewed for others. Skew matters because consecutive CLI releases disagree about whether identical history bytes are fatal, a warning, or invisible, so which copy loads can decide a workspace gate verdict. This package is a pure extension with no bin entry, and sixteen sibling packages import the same SDK at runtime while declaring the CLI only as a peer plus dev dependency."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: correctness,packaging
created_at: "2026-08-13T21:19:05.261Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T21:57:14.001Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-13T21:19:20.170Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-13T21:19:20.170Z"
author: codex
resolution: "Removed the CLI from dependencies so the host's peer copy is the only one that loads, and pinned the dev declaration exactly."
expected_result: Installing this package alongside any CLI version its declared peer range admits yields exactly one resolvable @unbrained/pm-cli.
actual_result: "Before the change the manifest permitted two independently-resolved copies. After it, the dependency declaration is gone, the peer declaration is what the host satisfies, and the guard in test/packaging.test.ts fails against the previous manifest shape and passes against the corrected one."
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  package-lock.json,project,resolves a single CLI copy at 2026.8.13
  package.json,project,pm CLI moved out of dependencies and the dev pin made exact
  test/packaging.test.ts,project,manifest guard proven to fail against the previous shape
tests[2]{command,path,scope}:
  "name=the host CLI is declared as a peer dependency and never as a runtime dependency,result=pass",test/packaging.test.ts,project
  "name=the host CLI dev dependency is pinned to an exact version rather than a range,result=pass",test/packaging.test.ts,project
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1003",project,upstream request for host-side detection of two resolvable CLI copies
close_reason: "Removed @unbrained/pm-cli from dependencies, leaving the peer declaration the host satisfies, and pinned the dev declaration exactly to 2026.8.13. A manifest guard in test/packaging.test.ts pins both properties and was proven to fail against the previous shape."
body: ""
